  {
   "id": "HW-POWER-001",
   "title": "Verify external servo power supply",
   "status": "in_progress",
   "hardware_required": true,
   "category": "power",
   "source": "docs/hardware_identification.md#bring-up-checklist-do-in-order-one-servo-at-a-time",
   "expected": {
    "voltage_v_nominal": 7.4,
    "supply_current_a_min": 5,
    "usb_only_allowed": false,
    "servo_protection_window_v": [
     4.0,
     8.0
    ],
    "lipo_2s_full_charge_exceeds_limit": true
   },
   "record": {
    "measured_voltage_v": 4.3,
    "supply_rating_a": null,
    "power_switch_location": null,
    "notes": "USB power only so far. Surprise: the FE-URT-2 DOES pass USB 5V to the servo bus -- the servo answers fully at 4.3V, so a silent bus is not the symptom of a missing supply and 'it answered' does not mean the supply is adequate. Below the 6-8.4V spec: no motion commanded. 7.4V >=5A still required. Servo's own voltage protection registers read 4.0-8.0 V (0x0f/0x0e), which is why it boots on USB. NOTE 8.0 V not 8.4: a freshly charged 2S LiPo exceeds the servo's own limit -- use a bench supply at 7.4 V."
   }
  },
